  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday morning through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 252 PM EDT Thu Aug 6 2026\n\nLittle change in our long-term outlook as conditions remain firmly \nlocked into the summertime regime. The influences of the Bermuda \nhigh will ensure a varying southerly flow and conditions favorable \nfor diurnal thunderstorms each day through early next week. This \nsetup will support elevated PWATs ranging from 1.5-2\" and PoP \nchances will remain in the 20-50% range over the area through the \nfirst of next week. Some of the storms may become strong with gusty \nwinds and localized flash flooding considerations. One hopeful \noutcome of the scattered afternoon convection is limiting the \nrise of high temperatures that are otherwise expected in the low \nto mid 90s outside of mountain areas by the weekend. As a result, \na Heat Advisory may be needed as indices rise into triple-digit \nterritory, particularly over central-eastern portions of our CWA.",
